  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:4900",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the targeting of Melanocyte protein PMEL through a complex network involving the P2X purinoceptor 1, TE-9, and LB2241-RCC. These entities are all targets of a common compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which suggests a shared mechanism of action. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the P2X purinoceptor, which in turn influences the activity of the target compounds, ultimately leading to the interaction with PMEL. The presence of multiple pathways converging on PMEL through different targets highlights a potential role in melanocyte function, possibly involving signaling pathways or cellular processes that are sensitive to these compounds. The integration of these findings suggests that Mollicellin N may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the P2X purinoceptor and its downstream targets, thereby influencing melanocyte-related processes.",
